A||N||8||burdell1||Headlight from Hell||||8
Z||000000||burdell1||09-15-1999||03:17 PM||||I am having a problem with the headlights on my '85GT. Namely, that they do not flip up or down. In trying to repair them, I finally got the pass. side one to come down, but that is about it. I replaced the isolator relay with a brand new one. I also replace the actuator relays on both sides with different (used) ones. Since fellow member Carrol was nice enough to provide me with some diiagrams i know which wires are supposed to get current. <P>However, most of them are not. I checked the fuses too. What I want to do (and tried) is to splice into similarly powered wires and use that for power. I've tried a couple, but it didn't exactly work right (my headlights blinked on and off like flashers.) Is this safe to do? Any suggestions? I'm trying to get this fixed before the snow flies.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||JetroGT||09-16-1999||02:04 AM||||I would search for a set of new head light motors. Or get some rebuilt ones. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||09-16-1999||02:07 AM||||If your junk yards don't have any Fieros, try looking at the older firebirds. Some of the model years had the same headlight motor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ggarsk||09-16-1999||02:39 AM||||It's the  early 80's Firebirds that the motors will fit Fiero's. The right side on the Firebird fits the left on the Fiero and visa versa.||||reg||7
Z||000004||burdell1||09-16-1999||08:53 AM||||There was one thing wrong with the driver's side headlight, but i fixed that. However, now both go down but won't go back up.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||09-17-1999||09:26 AM||||You probably need to rebuild the motors....they headlights will drop under even if the gear is stripped, but they wont go back up again.<P>Rebuilding the motors doesnt take very long, and you wont need to buy parts you just have to rotate the main gear 180 degrees.||||reg||1
Z||000006||burdell1||09-21-1999||11:25 AM||||Anybody got any other ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000007||TOM||09-21-1999||12:00 PM||||Its not the gear that goes bad. Its the drive coupling. It shreds then the pieces get caught between the gears and strips it. You will need to rotate the gear and replace the drive coupling. Or oh nevermind.||||reg||1
Z||000008||burdell1||09-21-1999||12:23 PM||||However, I'm pretty certain that it is not the motor...I'm certain it is the wiring....||||reg||1
